helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427				0	et	Järgnev tekst kirjeldab $[officename] BASICu teekide, moodulite ja dialoogide kasutamise põhitõdesid.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	et	$[officename] Basic provides tools to help you structuring your projects. It supports various "units" which enable you to group individual SUBS and FUNCTIONS in a Basic project.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148575				0	et	Teegid				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150011				0	et	Libraries serve as a tool for organizing modules, and can either be attached to a document or a template. When the document or a template is saved, all modules contained in the library are automatically saved as well.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151112				0	et	Teek võib sisaldada kuni 16 000 moodulit.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149262				0	et	Moodulid				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	et	A module contains SUBS and FUNCTIONS along with variable declarations. The length of the program that can be saved in a module is limited to 64 KB. If more space is required you can divide a $[officename] Basic project among several modules, and then save them in a single library.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152577				0	et	Dialoogi moodulid				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	et	Dialog modules contain dialog definitions, including the dialog box properties, the properties of each dialog element and the events assigned. Since a dialog module can only contain a single dialog, they are often referred to as "dialogs".				20200411 15:09:53
