helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153770				0	et	\<emph\>Date:\</emph\> String expression that contains the date that you want to calculate. The date can be specified in almost any format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153189				0	et	You can use this function to convert a date that occurs between December 1, 1582 and December 31, 9999 into a single integer value. You can then use this value to calculate the difference between two dates. If the date argument lies outside the acceptable range, $[officename] Basic returns an error message.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	et	In contrast to the DateSerial function that passes years, months, and days as separate numeric values, the DateValue function passes the date using the format "month.[,]day.[,]year".				20200411 15:09:53
