helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	et	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Any numeric expression that you want to calculate the natural logarithm for.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	et	The natural logarithm is the logarithm to the base e. Base e is a constant with an approximate value of 2.718282...				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	et	You can calculate logarithms to any base (n) for any number (x) by dividing the natural logarithm of x by the natural logarithm of n, as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420				0	et	Log n(x) = Log(x) / Log(n)				20200411 15:09:53
