helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3148522				0	et	Evaluates a list of arguments, consisting of an expression followed by a value. The Switch function returns a value that is associated with the expression that is passed by this function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154863				0	et	Süntaks:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3155934				0	et	Switch (Expression1, Value1[, Expression2, Value2[..., Expression_n, Value_n]])				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149119				0	et	Parameetrid:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3153894				0	et	The \<emph\>Switch\</emph\> function evaluates the expressions from left to right, and then returns the value that is assigned to the function expression. If expression and value are not given as a pair, a runtime error occurs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3153990				0	et	\<emph\>Expression:\</emph\> The expression that you want to evaluate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	et	\<emph\>Value:\</emph\> The value that you want to return if the expression is True.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3153346				0	et	In the following example, the \<emph\>Switch\</emph\> function assigns the appropriate gender to the name that is passed to the function:				20200411 15:09:53
