helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020404.xhp	0	help	par_id3153952				0	et	Use this attribute to check if a file or directory exists, or to determine all files and folders in a specific directory.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020404.xhp	0	help	par_id3159156				0	et	To check if a file exists, enter the complete path and name of the file. If the file or directory name does not exist, the Dir function returns a zero-length string ("").				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020404.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012	18			0	et	To generate a list of all existing files in a specific directory, proceed as follows: The first time you call the Dir function, specify the complete search path for the files, for example, "D:\\Files\\*.sxw". If the path is correct and the search finds at least one file, the Dir function returns the name of the first file that matches the search path. To return additional file names that match the path, call Dir again, but with no arguments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020404.xhp	0	help	par_id3147348				0	et	To return directories only, use the attribute parameter. The same applies if you want to determine the name of a volume (for example, a hard drive partition)				20200411 15:09:53
