helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153344				0	et	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/01030300.xhp\"\>BASICu programmi silumine\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159224				0	et	Katkestuspunktid ning sammukaupa käivitamine				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150682				0	et	You can check each line in your Basic program for errors using single step execution. Errors are easily traced since you can immediately see the result of each step. A pointer in the breakpoint column of the Editor indicates the current line. You can also set a breakpoint if you want to force the program to be interrupted at a specific position.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147303				0	et	Double-click in the \<emph\>breakpoint\</emph\> column at the left of the Editor window to toggle a breakpoint at the corresponding line. When the program reaches a breakpoint, the program execution is interrupted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155805	8			0	et	The \<emph\>single step \</emph\>execution using the \<emph\>Single Step\</emph\> icon causes the program to branch into procedures and functions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110				0	et	The procedure step execution using the \<emph\>Procedure Step\</emph\> icon causes the program to skip over procedures and functions as a single step.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153825				0	et	Katkestuspunkti omadused				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147574				0	et	The properties of a breakpoint are available through its context menu by right-clicking the breakpoint in the breakpoint column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3148473	10			0	et	You can \<emph\>activate\</emph\> and \<emph\>deactivate\</emph\> a breakpoint by selecting \<emph\>Active\</emph\> from its context menu. When a breakpoint is deactivated, it does not interrupt the program execution. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	et	Select \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> from the context menu of a breakpoint or select \<emph\>Breakpoints\</emph\> from the context menu of the breakpoint column to call the \<emph\>Breakpoints\</emph\> dialog where you can specify other breakpoint options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	et	The list displays all \<emph\>breakpoints\</emph\> with the corresponding line number in the source code. You can activate or deactivate a selected breakpoint by checking or clearing the \<emph\>Active\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3158407				0	et	The \<emph\>Pass Count\</emph\> specifies the number of times the breakpoint can be passed over before the program is interrupted. If you enter 0 (default setting) the program is always interrupted as soon as a breakpoint is encountered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	et	Katkestuspunkti eemaldamiseks programmist klõpsa \<emph\>Kustuta\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150439				0	et	Muutujate väärtuste jälgimine.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153368				0	et	You can monitor the values of a variable by adding it to the \<emph\>Watch\</emph\> window. To add a variable to the list of watched variables, type the variable name in the \<emph\>Watch\</emph\> text box and press Enter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3146986				0	et	The values of variables are only displayed if they are in scope. Variables that are not defined at the current source code location display ("Out of Scope") instead of a value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	et	You can also include arrays in the Watch window. If you enter the name of an array variable without an index value in the Watch text box, the content of the entire array is displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145749				0	et	If you rest the mouse over a predefined variable in the Editor at run-time, the content of the variable is displayed in a pop-up box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148618				0	et	The Call Stack Window				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154491				0	et	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_BASICIDE_STACKWINDOW_LIST\"\>Provides an overview of the call hierarchy of procedures and functions.\</ahelp\> You can determine which procedures and functions called which other procedures and functions at the current point in the source code.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150594				0	et	Käitusvigade loend				20200411 15:09:53
