helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	et	\<emph\>Result:\</emph\> Any numeric variable that contains the result of the comparison.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150448				0	et	\<emph\>Expression1, Expression2:\</emph\> Any expressions that you want to compare.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149562				0	et	When testing for equivalence between Boolean expressions, the result is \<emph\>True\</emph\> if both expressions are either \<emph\>True\</emph\> or \<emph\>False\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	et	In a bit-wise comparison, the Eqv operator only sets the corresponding bit in the result if a bit is set in both expressions, or in neither expression.				20200411 15:09:53
