helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156332				0	et	Time fields are not defined for dBASE databases and must be simulated. To internally display the time "14:00:00", a 5 is necessary.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3157965				0	et	"00:00:00" returns all records of a standard date field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146081				0	et	The database stores a date value internally using a combined date/time field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764				0	et	"45.79" does not return "45.79" although the \<emph\>entire field\</emph\> option is selected under \<emph\>Position\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155518				0	et	The view shown does not match what is stored internally. For example, if value 45.789 is stored in the database as a field of type Number/Double and the shown formatting is set to display only two decimals, "45.79" is only returned in searches with field formatting.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148481				0	et	In this case, standard formatting is formatting that refers to the internally stored data. It is not always visible to the user, especially if it is used for simulating data types (for example, time fields in dBASE databases). This depends on the database used and the individual data type. Searching with field formatting is appropriate if you only want to find what is actually shown. This includes fields of type Date, Time, Date/Time and Number/Double.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154507	31			0	et	However, searching without \<emph\>Apply field format \</emph\>is appropriate for larger databases with no formatting issues, because it is faster.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153355				0	et	If you are searching the values of check boxes, and \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> is on, then you will receive a "1" for marked check boxes, a "0" for unmarked check boxes, and an empty string for undefined (tristate) check boxes. If the search has been carried out with \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> set to off, you will see the language-dependent default values "TRUE" or "FALSE".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150995	119			0	et	If you use \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> when searching in list boxes, you find the text displayed in list boxes. If you do not use \<emph\>Apply field format,\</emph\> you will find the contents corresponding to the standard field format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150387				0	et	Tõstutundlik				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159267				0	et	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_CASE\"\>Specifies that upper and lower case are taken into consideration during the search.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145297				0	et	Tagasisuunas				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151249				0	et	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_BACKWARD\"\>Specifies that the search process will run in reverse direction, from the last to the first record.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152484				0	et	Algusest / lõpust				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156316				0	et	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_STARTOVER\"\>Restarts the search. A forward search restarts with the first record. A backwards search restarts with the last record.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163724				0	et	Metaavaldis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149255				0	et	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_WILDCARD\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Allows a search with a * or ? wildcard.\</ahelp\> You can use the following wildcards:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146317				0	et	Metamärgid				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150298				0	et	Tähendus				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919				0	et	Näide				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3158411				0	et	?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148874				0	et	for exactly one arbitrary character				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150365				0	et	"?loppy" returns "Floppy"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426				0	et	"M?ller" returns, for example, Miller and Moller				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148803				0	et	*				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156138				0	et	for 0 or more arbitrary characters				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146135				0	et	"*-*" returns "ZIP-Drive" and "CD-ROM"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155582				0	et	"M*er" returns all entries starting with an "M" and ending in "er" (for example, Miller, Moller, Mather)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145762				0	et	If you want to search for the actual characters ? or *, preface them with a backslash: "\\?" or "\\*". However, this is only necessary when \<emph\>Wildcard expression\</emph\> is enabled. When the option is not enabled, the wildcard characters are processed like normal characters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147130				0	et	Regulaaravaldis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150982				0	et	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_REGULAR\"\>Searches with regular expressions.\</ahelp\> The same regular expressions that are supported here are also supported in the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100000.xhp\" name=\"Find & Replace dialog\"\>Find & Replace dialog\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154718				0	et	Searching with regular expressions offers more options than searching with wildcard expressions. If you search with regular expressions, the following characters correspond to those used in searches with wildcards:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153705				0	et	Otsimine metaavaldiste abil				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149209				0	et	Otsimine regulaaravaldiste abil				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151045				0	et	?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150384				0	et	.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153793				0	et	*				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150428				0	et	.*				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150861				0	et	Olek				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154477				0	et	The \<emph\>State\</emph\> line shows the records returned by the search. If the search reaches the end (or the beginning) of a table, the search is automatically continued at the other end.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3163720				0	et	In very large databases, finding the record in reverse search order can take some time. In this case, the status bar informs you that the records are still being counted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147389				0	et	Otsi / Loobu				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	et	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_BTN_SEARCH\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Starts or cancels the search.\</ahelp\> If the search is successfully completed, the corresponding field in the table is highlighted. You can continue the search by clicking the \<emph\>Search\</emph\> button again. You can cancel a search process by clicking the \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145080				0	et	Sulge				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156166				0	et	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_BTN_CLOSE\"\>Closes the dialog. The settings of the last search will be saved until you quit \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151183				0	et	If several tables or forms are open, you can set different search options for each document. When you close the documents only the search options of the document last closed are saved.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	et	Disainirežiim sees/väljas				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151100				0	et	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170500.xhp\" name=\"Disainirežiim sees/väljas\"\>Disainirežiim sees/väljas\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150040				0	et	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SwitchControlDesignMode\"\>Toggles the Design mode on or off. This function is used to switch quickly between \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/04030000.xhp\" name=\"Design\"\>Design\</link\> and User mode. Activate to edit the form controls, deactivate to use the form controls.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153528				0	et	Please note the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01171000.xhp\" name=\"Open in Design Mode\"\>\<emph\>Open in Design Mode\</emph\>\</link\> function. If \<emph\>Open in Design Mode\</emph\> is activated, the document is always opened in Design mode, regardless of the state in which it is saved.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	et	If your form is linked to a database and you turn off the Design mode, the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0213.xhp\" name=\"Form Bar\"\>Form Bar\</link\> is displayed at the lower margin of the document window. You can edit the link to the database in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170201.xhp\" name=\"Form Properties\"\>Form Properties\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
