helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163822				0	et	Importimise nõuanded				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3155307				0	et	HTML-dokumenti importides teisendatakse järgnevad META-sildid automaatselt $[officename]-i andmeväljadeks: <META HTTP-EQUIV="REFRESH"...> ja <META NAME="..." ...>, kus NAME võrdub AUTHOR, CREATED, CHANGED, CHANGEDBY, DESCRIPTION, KEYWORDS või CLASSIFICATION.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3146146				0	et	Skriptid, kommentaarid ja META-sildid, mis asuvad otse enne silti TABLE, lisatakse tabeli esimesse lahtrisse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366				0	et	HTML-dokumendi päises leiduvad skriptid ja META-sildid imporditakse ja ankurdatakse dokumendi esimesse lõiku.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3152885				0	et	To set the options for importing HTML tags, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - HTML Compatibility\</emph\>. A known META tag contains either "HTTP-EQUIV" or "NAME", and are imported as $[officename] comments. The only exception is <META NAME="GENERATOR"...>, which is ignored.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163717				0	et	Eksportimise nõuanded				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3159180				0	et	Comments and script fields at the beginning of the first paragraph in a document are exported to the header of an HTML document. If the document begins with a table, the first paragraph in the first cell of the table is exported to the header of the HTML document.				20200411 15:09:53
