helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3154326				0	et	USHORT& nParam:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3159139				0	et	Input: Indicates, for which parameter the description is provided; parameters start at 1. If nParam is 0, the description itself is supposed to be provided in pDesc; in this case, pName does not have any meaning.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3147374				0	et	char* pName:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3145245				0	et	Output: Takes up the parameter name or type, for example, the word "Number" or "String" or "Date", and so on. Implemented in $[officename] Calc as char[256].				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3151020				0	et	char* pDesc:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148389				0	et	Output: Takes up the description of the parameter, for example, "Value, at which the universe is to be calculated." Implemented in $[officename] Calc as char[256].				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3145303				0	et	pName and pDesc are char arrays; implemented in $[officename] Calc with size 256. Please note that the space available in the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\> is limited and that the 256 characters cannot be fully used.				20200411 15:09:53
