helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145613				0	et	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_DOK:LB_DOKFORMAT\"\>Click the format that you want to apply to the selected field, or click "Additional formats" to define a custom format.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150138				0	et	\<variable id=\"datumuhrzeitformat\"\>When you click "Additional formats", the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Number Format\"\>\<emph\>Number Format\</emph\>\</link\> dialog opens, where you can define a custom format. \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154867				0	et	If you choose "Chapter number without separator" for a chapter field, the separators that are specified for chapter number in \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06060000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Outline numbering\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Outline numbering\</emph\>\</link\> are not displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156079				0	et	If you choose "chapter number" as the \<emph\>format\</emph\> for reference fields, only the number of the chapter heading containing the referenced object is displayed in the field. If the paragraph style for the chapter heading is not numbered, the field is left blank.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148682				0	et	The following number range formats are for paragraphs formatted with numbered or bulleted lists:				20200411 15:09:53
